    },
    "text": "About half of U.S. jobs are at high risk of being automated, according to a University of Oxford study, with the middle class disproportionately squeezed.",
    "translation": "牛津大学的一项研究显示，美国大约半数的工作岗位面临被自动化的极高风险，其中中产阶级受到的挤压尤为严重。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": {
      "structureType": "主谓宾补复合结构 + 独立介词短语插入 + with复合结构",
      "mainClause": "About half of U.S. jobs are at high risk of being automated...",
      "modifiers": "according to... 为介词短语作插入语表明出处；with the middle class disproportionately squeezed 为 with + 名词 + 过去分词构成的伴随独立主格结构，表补充说明伴随状态。",
      "corePattern": "be at high risk of doing sth.（面临做某事的高风险）；with + sb./sth. + done（随着/伴随着……被……）。"
    },
    "rawFields": {
